sections.content:
`kirolossedra` is the special same-name repository GitHub renders as the account's public profile README.

Its purpose is identity and technical self-presentation rather than application execution.

The page includes:

- a greeting;
- animated name text;
- profile-view tracking;
- a short engineering identity statement;
- a technology familiarity icon strip;
- GitHub streak statistics.

The README acts as a lightweight landing page for someone visiting the GitHub account.

Its user-facing functions are:

- identity;
- fast visual summary of technical interests;
- presentation of activity signals;
- branding through layout and dynamic imagery.

This is the earliest observed occurrence in the processed corpus so far of:

- a dedicated GitHub profile repository;
- dynamic README typing SVG integration;
- profile-view badge integration;
- consolidated skill-icon presentation;
- GitHub streak-stat presentation.

It also becomes the first processed repository whose meaningful maintenance clearly reaches 2026.
